*help_text e2r

*item e2r e2r_cfg_file
'The ESP-r model configuration file holds the definition '
'of the building/ plant to be simulated, including the name'
'of a [rcf] file which holds sets of information about the'
'Radiance files required to .'
'  cfg file  -> xx.rcf'
'               -> scene xx -> xx.rif'
'                           -> xx.mat  xx.sky  xx.rad'
'               -> scene yy -> yy.rif'
'                           -> yy.mat  yy.sky  yy.rad'
*enditem

*item e2r confirm_monitor_type
'Radiance was initially written when greyscale monitors were'
'common and it was necessary to confirm the users monitor'
'so that the correct display utility is used. Currently it'
'is used to force ximage to produce a dithered monochrome image if'
'there is insufficient colour depth.'
*enditem

*item e2r scene_config_file_name
'A scene configuration file (rcf) records high level attributes of each'
'of the scenes you create e.g. their intended use, associated'
'thermal zones, surfaces and edges associated with grids and the like.'
'  '
'  model.rcf  -> scene xx -> Glare, office'
'                         -> xx.rif xx,mat xx.sky xx.rad xx.grd'
'  '
'             -> scene yy -> Internal, passage'
'                         -> yy.rif yy.mat yy.sky yy.rad'
*enditem

*item e2r e2r_additional_overview
'The e2r module is designed to manage the creation of Radiance'
'visual models and replace the typical command line syntax of'
'the many applications in the Radiance suite. For many common tasks'
'you will not need to manually edit the Radiance descriptive files'
'or directly invoke Radiance commands.'
'  '
'Note that ESP-r does not know about changes you make to the'
'Radiance files created by e2r (your edits might be overwritten).'
'Make backups. One technique is to creat variants of scenes to'
'explore different visual aspects.'
'  '
'When you create a new scene or import an existing Radiance rif'
'file you are asked for its purpose. This sets parameters used'
'in the calculation process and controls user interactions e.g.'
'an interior rendering view asks which ESP-r zone the view point'
'is in, while a night scene will turn off the sun, set the ambient'
'light levels to match.'
'  '
'Radiance materials are grey-scale equivalents of ESP-r constructions'
'(one material for the inside face and one for the other face). These'
'will be generated as the ESP-r entities are created.'
'  '
'You can include an additional Radiance material file'
'in you scene and edit the polygon defintions to reference these.'
'  '
'As e2r exports geometric bodies it also creates a parallel set of'
'files for use if there is a Blender 3D representation of the ESP-r'
'model available.  If the source Wavefront file includes explicit'
'material layers then material properties will also be included.'
' '
'Lastly, those who are familiar with Radiance will have an advantage'
'and there are many resources on the web which can give you clues'
'about leveraging the facilities of e2r.'
*enditem

*item e2r furniture_file_name
'In order not to disturb files generated from a thermal'
'description it is sometimes useful to place miscel '
'furniture and fixtures in a separate file. If your ESP-r'
'model includes [predefined entities] or [visual entities]'
'these will already be included in the Radiance model.'
'  '
'You are given the option to browse the furniture and'
'fittings file or to open it up in a text editor.'
*enditem

*item e2r confirm_grid_point_edit
'If you want to alter the grid points say yes.'
*enditem

*item e2r octree_force_update
'The octree is a intermediate step between the Radiance input'
'files and the rendered image. Radiance should detect if the octree'
'needs recreated or not, although if you have a new sky file then'
'you must force Radiance to recreate the octree.'
*enditem

*item e2rform sky_def_local_file
'Supply a local file name (i.e. without a path) for the'
'sky definition.'
*enditem

*item e2rform sky_distribution_menu
'The attributes of the sky are managed by this facility:'
' '
'* Site Latitude: (imported from ESP-r) is in degrees.'
' '
'* Site Longitude: (imported from ESP-r) is degrees from'
'  a local reference meridian, east +ve, e.g. -4.1 for'
'  Glasgow relative to the Greenwich meridian.'
' '
'  Note this definition is different from that used by'
'  radiance.  Also, if a meridian other than the prime '
'  is defined in a sky file this will be reset to 0 and'
'  the longtitude difference calculated accordingly. '
' '
'* Year: this should be defined automatically and is used'
'  to sort out days of the week.'
' '
'* Date: change this to the date and time of the simulation,'
'  or leave it as the default.'
' '
'* Ground refl: this should be defined automatically.'
'  The average ground reflectance should be a fraction'
'  between 0.0 and 0.99.'
'  '
'* Sky: Toggle the type of sky conditions for the simulation. The'
'  CIE std overcast sky is the standard lighting design sky condition.'
' '
'* Generate sky description: Invokes Radiance to create the sky'
'  description file.'
' '
'* Display sky info: display the contents of the sky description'
'  file.'
*enditem

*item e2rform sky_not_CIE_menu
'You have requested a daylight factor calculation but the'
'sky type is not a CIE standard overcast sky. DF are not often'
'calculated with a different sky type.'
*enditem

*item e2rform sky_description_browse
'Browsing lists the file contents in the text feedback'
'area, editing spawns an editor with the file name.'
*enditem

*item e2rform sky_file_not_generated
'Radiance seems not to have been able to generate a sky'
'file. If you exit not the model will be incomplete.'
*enditem

*item e2rform e2r_outside_comp
'This menu defines the composition of the Radiance scene'
'in terms of materials and geometry. '
' '
'There are at least 3 files created - materials (surface '
'properties for entities from the ESP-r model), geometry'
'(of ESP-r entities as well as possible Wavefront file'
'sources), glazing (typically from ESP-r entities).'
' '
'After [generating] the files you may then manually'
'edit them as required to add in textures or colours.'
'Note: editing a named material will impact any geometric'
'entity referencing it. '
' '
'The [outer] face of internal partitions are EXCLUDED'
'because they are duplicates of the inner face of the '
'adjacent zone and cannot be seen in any event.  '
' '
'=============| |===========     '
'             | |                '
'    visible->| |<- visible face '
'    face     | |                '
'  zone a     | |   zone b       '
'             | |                '
'=============| |===========     '
'              |                 '
'               --- other sides of surfs '
'                   not seen and EXCLUDED '
'  '
'Options:'
' * Filter surfaces - ESP-r surfaces are passed to Radiance'
'   or all geometric entities are passed to Radiance.'
'  '
' * Fictitious surf - this value allows e2r to distinguish'
'   between normal glass and fictitious surfaces. You can'
'   state what glass transmission counts as fictitious.'
'  '
' * Groud tpology - the name of an esp-r file which holds'
'   the polygons and attributes of ground topology. This is'
'   not usually viewed within ESP-r but may be useful to provide'
'   a visual context for the Radiance image.'
'  '
' * Browse/edit - for each of the file types the browse will'
'   list out the contents of the file while edit will start a'
'   text editor.'
'  '
*enditem

*item e2rform e2r_outside_not_created
'The Radiance outside surfaces description file has not yet'
'been generated. You might lose information if you exit now.'
*enditem

*item e2rform writing_transpar_stuff
'Radiance typically holds optical properties in a separate'
'file and e2r bases what goes into this file from the optical'
'properties of ESP-r entities are.'
'  '
'Note: if you are also using Blender Wavefront files as a source'
'it is recommended that the Wavefront file excludes the transparent'
'bodies and uses the ESP-r glass surfaces and optical properties'
'instead.'
'  '
'Supply a local file name for the glazing file (i.e. without a path).'
'  '
'If your  model includes controls to optical properties you have the'
'option to create a Radiance model with an alternative set of optical'
'properties. If so you will be asked to supply a local file name'
'(i.e. without a path).'
'  '
'After streaming the optical properties for transparent surfaces'
'information about the surface properties of opaque bodiess'
'are written.
'  '
'And lastly the surface properties of internal (inward facing)'
'surfaces of the zones is streamed. You will be asked to supply'
'a local file name (i.e. without a path) for the inside composition.'
*enditem

*item e2rform precalculate_indirect_i
'Large sources of indirect illumination should have distributions'
'pre-calculated as this optimises the rendering process.'
' '
'The pre-calculation is achieved via the Radiance '
'utility mkillum.). You may be asked whether large surfaces'
'should be subdivided within mkillum.'
*enditem

*item e2rform writing_ies_xforms
'Light distributions fron fixtures can be imported from'
so-called IES data files.  Please specify a file name.'
*enditem

*item e2rvp view_form_creation
'Radiance renderings require a view point. Often several will be'
'needed for various tasks e.g. glare at different points in a'
'room and can be named to clarify their purpose and for inclusion'
'in the Radiance rif file.'
'  '
'For interior views you will be shown a plan view of the model'
'from which view point will be located. For outside views it'
'is possible to inherit the direction from the wire-frame view.'
'  '
'Other aspects are the direction and horizontal and vertical angle'
'of the view. These can be fine tuned in the Radiance interface and'
'saved to a view file which can then be imported. If you save a'
'number of view files these can be imported into different scenes'
'to save time.'
*enditem

*item e2rvp ext_MRTview
'Warning: The purpose of the currently selected scene is to create'
'external views. MRT sensors exist inside a model are inconsistent'
'with an external scene. Create a new scene for a MRT sensor position.'
*enditem

*item e2rvp view_definition_menu
'This menu selects the location and direction from which'
'the Radiance rendering or visual assement is taken.'
' '
'For external views the perspective feedback may be preferable'
'to the default view. Fine tune the wireframe view and then ask'
'to inherit this view. Otherwise fine tune the view in via'
'the Radiance interface and save the view to a file and then'
'import that. For example:'
' '
'To get an idea what the Radiance plan view attributes are'
'manually issue the command:'
' rad -V -vZl -n -s the_rif_file_name > plan.view'
'then in e2r ask to scan plan.view and preview to the'
'screen and use view commands to set the view position'
'as well as the -vo (near trim) and -va (aft trim) distances.'
' '
'For internal views the wireframe viewp is not appropriate.'
'Use the plan & elevation views. '
' '
'The eye point (x,y,z) can be edited and the display will update'
'to show the new position.'
'  '
'The View Direction can be changed by direct editing or using'
'the wireframe orientation.
' '
'The horizontal and vertical view angles can be changed by'
'direct editing.'
'  '
'The zones to include option controls the extent of the'
'view bounding box.'
'  '
'You can toggle between fisheye and perspective views. For a'
'fisheye view, view angles are always 180 degrees. For glare'
'assessments, fisheye views are highly recommended.'
*enditem

*item e2rvp eyepoint_editing
'The eyepoint is in metres in the coordinate system '
'of the site. '
' '
'To get an idea what the Radiance plan view attributes'
'are manually issue the command:'
' rad -V -v Zl -n -s the_rif_file_name > plan.view'
'then in e2r ask to scan plan.view and preview to the'
'screen and use view commands to set the view position'
'as well as the -vo (near trim) and -va (aft trim) distances.'
*enditem

*item e2rvp reflect_rad_view_in_per
'The wireframe view can be updated to approximate the Radiance'
'view (does not work well for internal views).'
*enditem

*item e2rvp edit_or_accept_current
'Editing is manual editing of the value. If it is ok then use the'
'accept current.'
'  '
'You will be given an option to pause and confirm the view.'
*enditem

*item e2rvp view_azimuth_edit
'The view azimuth 0= looking north, 90 =looking east.'
*enditem

*item e2rvp view_angle_edit
'The view angle is normally 60 deg.  The range'
'is 3. < x < 180.'
*enditem

*item e2rvp e2r_east_axis
'Adjust axis min and max to allow more distant view.'
*enditem

*item e2rvp e2r_north_axis
'Adjust axis min and max to allow more distant view.'
*enditem

*item e2rvp e2r_remind_to_save
'Recent changes in the view parameters might be lost'
'if you exit without saving the data. '
*enditem

*item radcfg scene_selection_list
'A project may involve a range of visual assessment tasks'
'each of which can be held in a separate [scene] definition.'
'  '
'You can select or manage (delete or add scenes as well as'
'making a variant of an existing scene) via this facility.'
'  '
'For example, if you have a scene supporting daylight factor'
'calculations in one space and want to carry out DF calculations'
'in another space make a variant which has the same attributes '
'but focused on a different space and with a grid specific to'
'space (i.e. the purpose of the variant is the same).'
'  '
*enditem

*item radcfg purpose_of_rif_scene
'The purpose of the scene guides the creation of the'
'Radiance files and computations as well as focusing the'
'interface.'
'  '
' External image - assumes you are looking at the model from'
'   the outside at a given date and time (or range of times).'
'  '
' Night external image - sets ambient light sources consistent'
'   with clear night sky, otherwise as external image.'
'  '
' Internal image - assumes a viewpoint within one of the zones'
'   in the model. You can add additional viewpoints in other'
'   zones as required (no need for a separate scene for each).'
'  '
' Glare - assumes a viewpoint within a zone and sets parameters'
'   and uses Radiance facilities for glare. Remember to set'
'   viewing parameters consisitent with this task (wide angle'
'   and horizontal). Again, you can define other viewpoints and'
'   do glare assessments based on that without creating additional'
'   scenes.'
'  '
' Daylight factors - focused on a zone of the model and a grid'
'   of points in the room and calculates daylight factors based'
'   on a standard overcast sky. If you want more than one grid'
'   i.e. for different spaces you will need multiple scenes.'
'  '
'  '
' Daylight lux - similar to daylight factors but determines the'
'   illuminance (lux) at each grid point based on a standard'
'   overcast sky. '
'  '
' Illuminance - focused on a zone of the model and a grid of'
'   points in the room and calculates illuminance at the points'
'   based on the current time and sky conditions.'
'  '
' Coupling - assumes a Radiance representation of one or more'
'   casual gain control sensors in a room and during simulation'
'   controls access to Radiance at each timestep to request the'
'   state of these sensors.'
'  '
' Daylight coefficient - Radiance supports a concept of pre-'
'   calculated coefficients from surfaces in the model to patches'
'   in the sky.'
*enditem

*item radcfg e2r_new_scene_name
'Many Radiance scenes may be created for a given ESP-r thermal'
'model. For example, one scene may be of the building exterior'
'and others could be for internal images of a zone or for a glare'
'assessment. Each scene can have multiple viewpoints.'
'  '
'The scene prefix (one word) is used in the creation of'
'the rif file name and as a root name for the description,'
'view, octree and image files. It is also used in selection'
'lists (i.e. clear names speeds up selection).  '
'  '
'There is also a descriptive phrase to identify the scene.'
*enditem

*item radcfg df_stay_focused
'As calculations proceed the daylight factors shown on the'
'grid will be refreshed. The wireframe view can be of the'
'focus zone or all zones.'
*enditem

*item radcfg create_scene_interactive
'Radiance desktop supports the creation of scenes with minimal'
'input i.e. given a purpose it sets a number of attributes.'
' '
'You can later adapt the attributes of the scene and the'
'computational parameters as needed.'
*enditem

*item radcfg pick_focus_zone
'Pick a zone as the focus for the assessment. For an [internal]'
'or [glare] scene this helps in setting up the viewpoint. For'
'daylight factor calculations it is used when setting up'
'the grid of points where calculations will be made. '
' '
*enditem

*item radcfg distance_to_df_grid
'The grid points are offset from the chosen surface (either'
'inward or outward along the surface normal.'
'  '
'You will be asked to select an edge (via two vertex'
'indicies. The grid will be formed in rows parallel '
'to that selected edge.'
*enditem

*item radcfg df_grid_density
' A bounding box is created for the selected surface.'
' The grid is specified by intersection points of lines'
' parallel and perpendicular to the selected edge.'
' The grid lines are equally spaced, starting half the'
' width of a space from the edge, e.g. '
'      ||     |          |'
'      ||     |          |'
'      ||<--->|<-------->|'
'      || x/2 |     x    |'
'      ||     |          |'
'     edge    |          grid line 2'
'           grid line 1'
'  '
'After specifying the grid density you will be asked for the'
'name of a file which will hold the grid points created.'
'Give the name of this file without a path.'
*enditem

*item radcfg e2r_RIF_file_name
'A RIF (Raidance Input File) specifies the composition'
'of the problem for Radiance as well as parameters for'
'images quality and calculation parameters. '
' '
'Existing files will be scanned, otherwise you are guided'
'in the creation of new scenes. '
*enditem

*item radcfg e2r_WF_file_name
'Radiance entities can be created from a Wavefront obj file.'
'e2r will do the conversion to a Radiance mesh if you give'
'it the name of the Wavefront file.'
'  '
'Note: the obj2mesh Radiance application is used for this.'
'e2r will do the conversion AND it is a good idea to check'
'the feedback to see if there were any errors.'
*enditem

*item radcmds e2r_proceed_with_sim
'You can postpone the visual simulation if you need to adjust'
'calculation parameteres or add a viewpoint.'
' '
'Visual simulations can take several minutes, if not hours to'
'complete - look in the command window behind the e2r tool to'
'track progress.'
'  '
'If the scene purpose is a glare study there are several'
'steps to the glare process so watch the process in the'
'command window.'
*enditem

*item radcmds standard_times_of_day
'Pick a season/ time for the sky. This is a quick way to get an'
'image which has the sun in typical locations in the sky (morning'
'afternoon and winter and summer).'
*enditem

*item radcmds single_time_or_sequence
'Rendering can be for one moment or at intervals e.g. every'
'1, 10 or 15 or 20 minutes during a period of a day.'
'You can adjust the parameters needed to create a set of images'
'(gif or tif or jpg) which can be combined to form an amimation.'
' '
'If you specify a period from 8h00 to 9h00 at a 20 minute'
'interval on the 69th day of the year there will be four files'
'created (.hdr) and converted to gif files via the Radiance'
'utility ra_gif or tiff files via the ra_tiff utilty or to jpg'
'files via the Imagemagick convert utility.'
'  '
'You can then use a tool such as gimp or gifsicle or convert '
'to combine the separate files into an animation.'
' '
'For example: '
'  gifsicle -l1 -d100 69*.gif >animation.gif'
'will take all of the gif files that start with 69 and com-'
'bine them into a file animation.gif with a 100ms delay between'
'frames. This can be viewed in a web browser or via a utility'
'named animate (part of the Imagemagick tool set).'
'  or '
'  convert -delay 20 -loop 0 *.jpg animated.gif'
' '
'NOTE: convert tends to darken when converting from hdr to jpg so'
'you might need to alter the command to:'
'   convert -brightness-contrast 20x-20 -loop 0 *.jpg animated.gif'
'to increase brighness by 20% and decrease contrast by 20%.'
*enditem

*item radcmds render_to_screen_or_file
'Rendering can only be directed to screen (where you can adjust'
'the visualisation parameters interactively). Once you are happy'
'with the rendering you can get a higher resolution rendering'
'via the file which is created.'
'  '
'If running on Windows you should choose file option.'
*enditem

*item radcmds end_time_of_animation
'The end of the animation is assumed to be on the same'
'day and must be less than 24.0'
'  '
'The time increment is usually set as a compromise between'
'the visual jump between views and computation time. '
'  '
'The image frame size is a compromise between the'
'visual detail and and computation time. '
'  '
'Once the sequence of images has been created you can use'
'a tool such as gimp or gifsicle or convert to combine the'
'separate files into an animated gif. There may be 3rd party'
'tools that can take a set of images and create a movie file.
' '
'For example: '
'  gifsicle -l1 -d100 69*.gif >animation.gif'
'will take all of the gif files that start with 69 and com-'
'bine them into a file animation.gif with a 100ms delay between'
'frames. This can be viewed in a web browser or via a utility'
'named animate (part of the Imagemagick tool set).'
'  or '
'  convert -delay 20 -loop 0 *.jpg animated.gif'
' '
'NOTE: convert tends to darken when converting from hdr to jpg so'
'you might need to alter the command to:'
'   convert -brightness-contrast 20x-20 -loop 0 *.jpg animated.gif'
'to increase brighness by 20% and decrease contrast by 20%.'
*enditem

*item radcmds overwrite_existing_pic
'The image processing tends to [hang] when trying to'
'overwrite an existing image. Choose a different root'
'name for the image(s) if you can.'
'  '
*enditem

*item radcmds e2r_falsecolour
'False colour images with lux contours can be defined. You'
'are asked about the range of expected lux within the image'
'as well as the number of contours to plot.'
' '
'You may need to experiment to find appropriate parameters.'
'Note: false colour images tend to work better if there are'
'internal light sources in the scene.'
*enditem

*item radcmds e2r_df_convergence
'The calculations will start with one ambient bounce and'
'gradually increase the number of bounces until the change'
'is less than a value (convergence criteria). The smaller'
'the value the longer the calculations will take. '
' '
'If the display freezes it may be because the underlying'
'rtrace calculations are hung. You may have to kill that'
'process. '
*enditem

*item radcmds e2r_confusion
'Sometimes Radiance gets confused. This is one place'
'where starting again can correct this. Also check the'
'feedback in the command window.'
*enditem

*item radcmds e2r_file_overwrite
'Daylight factors or lux values are written to a file. If'
'this file already exists you have a chance to save the past'
'by giving a different file name.'
*enditem

*item radcmds e2r_lux_convergence
'The calculations will strart with one ambient bounce and'
'gradually increase the number of bounces until the change'
'is less than a value (convergence criteria). The smaller'
'the value the longer the calculations will take. '
' '
'If the display freezes it may be because the underlying'
'rtrace calculations are hung. You may have to kill that'
'process. '
*enditem

*item rifform e2r_scene_files_menu
'This menu selects the scene description files to be used'
'in the assessment as well as setting a number of calculation'
'parameters.'
' '
'Radiance will use these parameters. If other details of'
'the rif file need to be manually adjusted you can look at'
'the contents of the rif file or edit those contents and'
'then re-scan the edited file.'
'  '
'You can test the rif file creation without proceeding with'
'a full calculation.'
'  '
'Remember to save the RIF file to record any changes you'
'have made.'
*enditem

*item rifform image_quality_options
'Image quality sets a number of command parameters and can'
'influences processing time.  Most of the time a medium'
'quality image will suffice (and there are opts '
'which can get close to higher quality image without the
'waiting-for-the-paint-to-dry implied by high quality).'
*enditem

*item rifform e2r_detail_level_options
'Detail level: Use low for zones with few surfaces (ie'
'as in a thermal problem), use Medium if furnature and'
'objects, use High if lots of detail and textures. '
*enditem

*item rifform e2r_light_var_options
'Light level variability: Use Low for zones which are '
'uniformally lit by lighting fixtures, Medium if there'
'is diffuse skylight and High for direct sunlight.'
*enditem

*item rifform e2r_light_system_options
'Artificial) lighting is less sensitive to the number of'
'bounces while natural lighting is best with one or two'
'or even bounces. More bounces increases compute time'
'greatly!'
'  '
'As a basic guide when previewing use one bounce and then'
'increase for final rendering.'
*enditem

*item rifform e2r_pixel_size_options
'Set overall image width in pixels (smaller numbers '
'process more quickly). The height and thus image'
'pixel aspect are automatically set from the view'
'data (-vh and -vv options).'
*enditem

*item rifform e2r_penumbras_options
'Penumbras (soft shadows) in image is processor intensive'
'and some users prefer this.'
*enditem

*item rifform track_progress_options
'Computations can take a moment to several hours - so '
'a % completion report is available. '
*enditem

*item rifform e2r_viewpoint_options
'Initial/simple view points are built up based on a  '
'bounding box defined by minimimum & maximum X Y Z  '
'coordinates of the focus zone or of the whole buildig.'
'Usually this will be correctly set automatically.'
*enditem

*item rifform e2r_ambient_file_name
'This holds temporary information on ambient light'
'when a number of viewpoints are to be generated of '
'the same scene.  NOT desirable othewise. '
*enditem

*item rifform e2r_options_file_name
'This holds additional calculation option commands'
'in a file. This is for experts.'
*enditem

*item rifform e2r_pic_root_name
'This is the root name for pictures created with [rad]'
*enditem

*item rifform e2r_RIF_file_name
'A RIF (Raidance Input File) specifies the composition'
'of the problem for Radiance as well as parameters for'
'images quality and calculation parameters. '
' '
'If the file given exists it will be read in, if not '
'a new one will be created with typical defaults. '
*enditem

